oration: underline; color: #006699;" rel=3D"noopener">fascinating piece of =
analysis</a> (in short, a mix of suction fans and thrusters). It=E2=80=99s =
a reminder that, despite his deeply questionable politics, Musk can be a fo=
rce for progress.&nbsp;</span>
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><br>
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">Raqual, a single m=
other and nurse, is in an absurd position. She makes a modest living but if=
 she picks up an extra shift, she will keep only 23 pence of every extra po=
und she earns. She faces a tax rate that even Britain=E2=80=99s highest ear=
ners couldn=E2=80=99t imagine in their worst nightmares. And yet this is a =
common trap baked into the system by Britain=E2=80=99s broken welfare state=
. This week The Times launched our Welfare Inquiry to examine these problem=
s and how to fix them. Today, as the first tranche of our coverage comes to=
 an end, <a href=3D"https://link.thetimes.com/click/47970560.376114/aHR0cHM=
6Ly93d3cudGhldGltZXMuY29tL3VrL3dlbGZhcmUtaW5xdWlyeS9hcnRpY2xlL3dlbGZhcmUtY2=
